From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:12:34 -0400
Subject: remember which Space each tab was in

Spaces came back after a restart but their tabs did not: everything landed in
whichever Space was active. Each tab now carries its Space in the session's
per-tab extra data, written whenever the tab joins or moves Space.

Reading it back has an ordering problem. A tab is rebuilt before it belongs to
any window, so there is no SpaceModel to tell at that point. The id is parked on
the WebContents as user data -- the same thing glic and send-tab-to-self do a
line above -- and collected the first time anything asks which Space the tab is
in, which is exactly when the model already assigns unseen tabs.

A tab whose Space did not come back joins the active one rather than keeping an
id that matches nothing, which would leave it invisible in every Space.

Why: Spaces that come back empty are not the arrangement the user left.
Removable when: the session service can express tab sets itself.
